      formula: "Principle: income policy instruments, from voluntary guidelines to mandatory wage and price freezes, stabilize the price level when demand policies fail.",
      substitution: "A freeze is the mandatory end of the income policy range.",
      calculation: "By directly holding wages and prices below free market levels, the freeze restrains cost and price rises that demand policies could not curb.",
