  summary: "Income policy uses economy-wide wage and price controls, from voluntary guidelines to mandatory freezes, especially when inflation resists fiscal and monetary cures. In free markets the wage rate is set by labour supply and demand under competitive conditions; the minimum wage is a legal price floor protecting workers from low pay and supporting fewer-poverty, more-equal societies. Price ceilings below equilibrium create shortages, and price floors above equilibrium create surpluses, shift surplus from consumers to producers and create deadweight loss.",
